# The official Serve image digest pins the full transitive runtime. These are
# the overlay packages applied on top of it.
#
# The overlay used to hold `docling-core` BACK: the v1.30.0 base shipped 2.91.0
# and this pinned 2.90.0, so that the jobkit heading-hierarchy fix would be the
# only library change a behaviour difference could be attributed to.
#
# That hold is now impossible, and this is the entry that says why: docling-slim
# 2.121.0 declares `docling-core>=2.91.0`, and the Dockerfile runs `pip check`.
# The engine takes the core with it. So the comment's own instruction — re-measure
# the Stage A-D structure evidence when Core moves — came due and was paid: the
# A/B on `tests/integration/fixtures/docling-quality/` is what accepted 2.92.0.
#
# What moves with it, and what the measurement was watching for:
#   - core 2.92.0 serialises markdown with GFM line breaks (#721) and lets the
#     chunker carry content layers past the document (#593). Both change text,
#     which moves chunk boundaries.
#   - docling 2.121.0 descends into a content control that holds an image
#     (#3952) — docx is more than half of what this service converts.
#   - docling 2.120.0 infers PDF heading level from font weight, slant and case
#     (#3984), which is the capability `DOCLING_MCP_PDF_HEADING_HIERARCHY` asks
#     for per conversion.
docling-slim[standard,service-client,models-remote,format-opendocument]==2.121.0
docling-core==2.92.0
grpcio==1.67.1
